**Summary:**
(1) The paper proposes a novel framework for semi-supervised semantic segmentation, namely adaptive equalization learning;

(2) The paper proposes two data augmentation strategies including adaptive Copy-Paste and CutMix to give more chance for under-performing categories to be copied or cut;

(3) The paper presents an adaptive equalization sampling strategy to encourage pixels from under-performing categories to be sufficiently trained;

(4) A simple yet effective re-weighting strategy is proposed to alleviate the noise problem in semi-supervised learning;

(5) Experimental results illustrate the effectiveness of the paper.
